ledger entry 1: DESI DR1 VAC 'gfinder' (Yang-type halo-based groups; PUBLIC, touched)
   files: DESIDR9.y1.v1_group.fits (5.6 GB), _galaxy.fits (8.4 GB), i*.fits (3.2 GB)
   remote FITS headers read: N_groups = 99,599,634 ; N_gal-group links = 134,731,580
   head parsed locally: 535,611 rows | RICH>=50: 7,274 | RICH>=100: 1,273 | logM max 15.47
   -> >~1,273 clusters with >=100 (spec+photo-z) members, thousands with >=50. CAVEAT: RICH
      mixes photo-z members (MAG_Z<21); spec-only membership is smaller. Redshift side only:
      NO internal-sigma columns in this VAC. Per-member v_los precision ~10-30 km/s (Redrock).

ledger entry 2: DESI DR1 VAC 'extragalactic-dwarfs' (PUBLIC, touched)
   desi_dwarfs_y1_catalog.fits: N = 647,241 dwarfs (Mstar <~ 1e9 Msun), 0.001<z<0.5
   columns verified: Z, MU_R, SHAPE_R, LOGM_CIGALE... (80 cols; head sample: ~4.5% MU_R>24 LSB-like)
   -> the largest homogeneous spectroscopic DWARF sample ever (redshifts + structure), i.e. the
      CARRIER-IDENTIFICATION + phase-tagging feed. NO internal sigma (below DESI resolution).
ledger entry 3: HeCS (Rines+2013, VizieR J/ApJ/767/15; PUBLIC, downloaded)
   clusters: 58 (z~0.1-0.3, X-ray selected) | redshift rows: 22,680
   members per cluster: median 173, range 61-461 (column Nm)
   per-member cz precision: median e_cz = 36 km/s -> superb for PPS tagging
ledger entry 4: HeCS-SZ (Rines+2016, J/ApJ/819/63; PUBLIC, downloaded)
   clusters: 123 (Planck SZ-selected, sigma_cl 300-1200 km/s) + 11,585 new redshifts (table2,
   counted via TAP). Same character: member cz for phase space; no internal sigma.
ledger entry 5: HeCS-omnibus (Sohn+2020, J/ApJ/891/129; PUBLIC, downloaded)
   clusters: 227 (z<=0.29) | SUM(Nmem) = 52,415 spectroscopic members (median 180/cluster,
   max 1209) | SUM(N200) = 22,091. BCG internal sigma (table3): 227 BCGs, e_sigma ~ 3-8 km/s --
   but BCGs are the MOST adiabatic-dead objects in the sky (y~0.01): zero carrier value.
   THE flagship phase-space compilation: caustic membership, R200, sigma_cl per cluster.
ledger entry 6: GalWCat19 (Abdullah+2020, J/ApJS/246/2; SDSS-DR13-based; PUBLIC, downloaded)
   clusters: 1800 (z<0.2) | member galaxies: 34,471 (~19/cluster median-ish)
   member rows carry (RA,DE,z,ClID): phase-space side only.
ledger entry 7: CAIRNS (Rines+2003, J/AJ/126/2152; PUBLIC, downloaded)
   clusters: 9 nearby massive (A1656/Coma etc.) | galaxies: 19,796
   the classic deep infall-region survey -> best per-cluster caustic profiles at low z.

